{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108680","id":2671624490,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6fPcEq","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108680","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108680.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108680.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108680","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108680/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108680/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108680/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b025bfae7ab59db9a88050eef690fe994c107a8d","number":108680,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add `test_ray` function: a version of intersect_ray that has optional result parameter","user":{"login":"snorkel456","id":1427129,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjcxMjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1427129?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456","html_url":"https://github.com/snorkel456","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snorkel456/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Note (22/07/2025):\r\n- After searching around other PRs I've found that this is probably redundant once struct are easier to add (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108503). The performance gain is going to be similar to the struct version, but the struct version doesn't require pre-allocating a result object. So depending on the time frame this PR might not be useful.\r\n\r\n\r\nProblem:\r\n- When profiling my game I found that most time in intersect_ray is spend on creating and filling in the Dictionary that is returned.\r\n- Often in my game code I only need to know if the ray hit anything and don't care about the data in the Dictionary.\r\n- My game uses raycasts for everything from bullets, AI to level generation, any speedup would be great.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n- User has to pass a OPTIONAL result object to the function\r\n- This change mimics how physicsserver3d body_test_motion is implemented.\r\n- bonus: result object can be preallocated and reused similar to PhysicsRayQueryParameters3D (no C# garbage)\r\n\r\nFirst tests give a big performance speedup in both GDscript and C# when ray hits a surface. (~5x faster in release export)\r\nIt is even slightly faster when no result object is passed.\r\n\r\n(These tests reuse the result object instead of allocating a new one each time. This is also how I use PhysicsRayQueryParameters3D in a game project.)\r\n\r\n\r\nExample usage:\r\n\r\nAs replacement for intersect_ray with better performance:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar params = PhysicsRayQueryParameters3D.create(Vector3.ZERO, Vector3(0, 0, 100))\r\nvar ray_result = PhysicsTestRayResult3D.new()\r\nif (space_state.test_ray(params, ray_result)):\r\n    print(\"position: \", ray_result.position)\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nAs test to see if ray is blocked\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar params = PhysicsRayQueryParameters3D.create(Vector3.ZERO, Vector3(0, 0, 100))\r\nvar hit := space_state.test_ray(params)\r\n```\r\n\r\nTodo:\r\n- update docs for added function & class\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330068,"